REGEDIT4

; VirtualDJ pairs a controller with its ASIO driver by exact name, and its
; DDJ-FLX10 definition looks for "DDJ-FLX10 ASIO" -- the name the AlphaTheta
; driver registers on Windows. The subkey name under HKLM\Software\ASIO is
; only the list/display name, so aliasing PipeASIO's CLSID under that name is
; all VirtualDJ needs to treat PipeASIO as the controller's driver.
;
; pipeasio-register registers the same CLSID under HKLM\Software\ASIO\PipeASIO,
; so both names appear in VirtualDJ's ASIO list and resolve to one driver. The
; virtualdj launcher imports this file after running pipeasio-register.

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\Software\ASIO\DDJ-FLX10 ASIO]
"CLSID"="{2D3CA9E2-1193-4C5D-B5FD-38798F3DC074}"
"Description"="DDJ-FLX10 ASIO"
